Maintainer: Alp Berkman <alpberkman@gmail.com>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13), pkg-config, libx11-dev
Standards-Version: 4.6.2
Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: swallow
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Suggests: jq
Description: swallow a terminal into a launched GUI app's window
 swallow hides the terminal a GUI application was launched from while
 that application's window is open, and restores the terminal's
 position and size when the window closes -- or, with --remain, moves
 the terminal to wherever the window ended up instead, or, with
 --kill, closes the terminal instead of restoring it.
 .
 This package installs three commands: swallow, the C/X11
 implementation for Openbox and other reparenting ICCCM/EWMH window
 managers; swallow-i3, a separate implementation for i3/sway built on
 their IPC (needs jq); and swallow-auto, which picks between the two
 based on which window manager is actually running. Optional shell
 integration for wrapping a fixed list of GUI apps so they're launched
 through swallow-auto automatically is shipped as
 /usr/share/swallow/shell-integration.sh but not wired into any
 ~/.bashrc automatically -- see /usr/share/doc/swallow/README.md.
